  "id": "trimmed-mean",
  "term": "trimmed mean",
  "definition": "A trimmed mean is a measure of central tendency found by ordering the data, removing an equal percentage of the lowest and highest values, and then averaging what remains. It is considered a robust average and typically falls between the mean and the median.",
